  "body": "When you create a user using `/register`, you only need to use the localpart because the server will helpfully fill in its own domain name, and return you in the response the fully-qualified user ID. This avoids clients having to remember or know the canonical name for the server.\n\nIt might be handy to support a `POST` URL to `/directory/room`, instead of [`PUT /directory/room/{roomAlias}`](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.12/client-server-api/#put_matrixclientv3directoryroomroomalias) to assist in creating a room alias when you only know the desired localpart, as it avoids the client needing to remember the full domain name which would otherwise be needed when {{PUT}}ing it.\n\n(Imported from https://matrix.org/jira/browse/SPEC-184)\n\n(Reported by @leonerd)\n",
